{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202324-sell-me-on-the-dragon-blooded","id":1202324,"title":"Sell me on the Dragon-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-02T16:02:31-07:00","id":1202324,"title":"Sell me on the Dragon-Blooded","content":"Ok, I'm not actually going to ask you to sell me on the Dragon-Blooded; I've been a big fan of DBs in general and the Realm in particular since 1E.<br /> <br /> What I <i><b>am</b></i> asking is for a bit of insight into DBs and dynasts before I make a decision about backing the kickstarter. I'll get right to my concern: that the Dragon-Blooded will be primarily defined by their utter inferiority (spiritually, martially, etc.) to the other exalts of the setting and that the Realm will be a baby-eating monster machine with no purpose or redeeming features other than to sit around being horrible and waiting for someone more powerful (a Solar, a Lunar, or whatever) to kick it over and make something better. <br /> <br /> There are themes about the Dragon-Blooded that I've always found very interesting... but it's hard for me to get into those themes, playing a heroic dynast or Immaculate monk, if the stuff that I don't personally enjoy all that much is at the forefront. I'm not saying that those things are bad per se, just that the aren't for me.<br /> <br /> I've follow the threads here about the Kickstarter, but I thought to start my own thread to get some perspective on the newest incarnation of the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:07:21-07:00","id":1202326,"title":"","content":"I'm new to Exalted with 3e, though I've glanced through some products of both previous editions. I've never been interested in Dragon-blooded because they seemed lame to me because I thought they played second fiddle to everyone else and are just there to bolster the danger the Realm poses.<br /> <br /> The new book changed all that for me.<br /> <br /> Dragon-blooded are badass. Exalting, no matter what kind of Exalt, is fucking badass and you're a <i>hero</i>. The world is yours to inherit. There's no hiding in the shadows here. Their political power might have been founded on a Sidereal lie, but their struggles, victories, tragedies, and romances are just as real as anyone's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:07:38-07:00","id":1202327,"title":"","content":"The short version is all of your fears are absent and all of your interesting themes are prominent.<br /> <br /> Edit: Additionally, if you back it for $5, you'll be able to download the manuscript (that is, the full text, released in batches over the course of the KS) that's yours to keep, even if you dislike what you read and withdraw your pledge at the end. So there's nothing stopping you from just reading the book now and determining if you want to back it. Rich and team encourage this behavior. They want to earn your pledge, not make you assume it from others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:37:31-07:00","id":1202335,"title":"","content":"My endorsements might be a little bit spoiler-y, but I can't think of a more discrete way to endorse the book within parameters that you have laid down, so proceed at your own leisure.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202324-sell-me-on-the-dragon-blooded#post1202324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that the Dragon-Blooded will be primarily defined by their utter inferiority (spiritually, martially, etc.) to the other exalts of the setting</div> </div> </div> </div>The opening fiction depicts a Dragon Blooded Sworn Kinship coming together in the wake of a devastating attack on their Wyld Hunt, and chasing down the Solar and Lunar that did it, killing one and taking the other prisoner.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe first chapter, among other things, refers to groups of Dragon Blooded that had sovereignty even in the First Age.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe second chapter gives Houses of the Scarlet Dynasty a lot of achievements in the fields of government, politics, conquest, business and the occult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Realm will be a baby-eating monster machine with no purpose or redeeming features other than to sit around being horrible and waiting for someone more powerful (a Solar, a Lunar, or whatever) to kick it over and make something better.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Realm is still not exactly nice, but it's rather pretty, and it does possess things that are to the benefit of people that live there.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:43:11-07:00","id":1202338,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-Blooded are the most inherently colorful Host of Exalted in the setting, beating out even the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> In no small part because jade comes in five colors and Terrestrisl Exalted have neutral Resonance with everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:48:02-07:00","id":1202339,"title":"","content":"There are also a bunch of options for non-realm dragonblooded like Prasad and Forest Witches and Lookshy that have decent support in the core and are getting extended writeup in Heirs of the Shogunate due to stretch goals. <br /> <br /> The Prasadi are especially cool because they're a semi-independent state where DBs are worshipped as gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:55:06-07:00","id":1202341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202324-sell-me-on-the-dragon-blooded#post1202324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Realm will be a baby-eating monster machine with no purpose or redeeming features other than to sit around being horrible</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually, I can think of one way to respond to this that doesn't give away too much of what is in the book:<br /> <br /> \u200bThe book portrays some groups of the Dragon Blooded of the Realm as having sincere agendas and ideologies concerning the function of the Realm and their place therein. When I say &quot;some groups&quot;, I'm not talking about a token good guy or two, just that it's not the focus of every corner of their society. It's a reasonably even mix.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe pursuit of these beliefs will lead to them doing some nice things, and some terrible things that they have a different perspective on. The potential for good is not incidental, even if it's not the one-and-only that can arise from them doing their thing.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt should also be noted that, conversely, there are aspects of the Realm's seedy underbelly that go a bit darker than they have before, but even the portrayal of that is handled with nuance and sophistication.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's complex, but it's rich, and I would say that to dig into it in detail would be rewarding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T17:06:49-07:00","id":1202348,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've yet to see anything in the text that really implies DBs are inferior to other Exalts. The closest would be the opening fiction where it mentions 2 anathema did severe damage to a Wyld Hunt before escaping, but even then the part about the bond afterwords makes it feel less, &quot;Dragonblood are inferior to other exalts&quot; and more &quot;Stupid, these are Anathema, these are dangerous monsters and we didn't use the bond. Of course you're going to get wrecked if you tie your arms behind your back before wrestling a bear.&quot; <br /> <br /> As for the Realm, well I mean there's bad stuff in there, but they're nobles. To clarify there was a novel in 2nd where a Wyld Hunt was looking for an Anathema and an innkeeper who was questioned said he didn't know. There wasn't any indication that the innkeeper was lying, but the fire aspect immediately responded by killing the man and setting the inn on fire,* and the rest of the hunt pretty much treated it like the mortal had it coming. That hasn't been the indication we've gotten so far in the books. Not saying you're not going to get Dynastic pricks, but so far it feels much more like standard noble issues in a fantasy setting just that the nobles tend to be demigods as opposed to random people from a noble house.<br /> <br /> *Admittedly being a fire aspect meant that both of those could be accomplished in the same sword swing, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T17:11:55-07:00","id":1202352,"title":"","content":"The Realm Houses have one or two definite bad guy factions, but these mostly serve to provide antagonists for a realm-based game where there's no solars involved at all. Hell, one of them actually works as a solar <i>ally</i>.<br /> <br /> So the main baby eating is there for <i>other dragon blooded</i> to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T17:22:15-07:00","id":1202365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202324-sell-me-on-the-dragon-blooded?p=1202352#post1202352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm Houses have one or two definite bad guy factions, but these mostly serve to provide antagonists for a realm-based game where there's no solars involved at all. Hell, one of them actually works as a solar <i>ally</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's one approach. I see compelling reasons to play as them, and not just simply the notion of playing the villains.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that what matters, for every quarter of the Scarlet Dynasty, is that they're <i>motivated</i>. They're not just resting on their laurels benefiting from their status as Princes of the Earth, barring the intrusion of the possibility of civil war; they have world views that shape things that they're trying to achieve in the future. So that even when there's bad on an institutional level, it's bad with a motivation that can be understood and related to, rather than just because they're irredeemable monsters who thrive off of doing bad things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T17:40:27-07:00","id":1202369,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, it's not entire houses that are bad eggs.<br /> <br /> Like, the Ragara elders are up to some nasty shit. The younger members, who you'll end up playing, have no idea. <br /> <br /> So you can play a heroic Ragara scion who ends up being all &quot;omg grandpa wtf are you doing?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T20:48:00-07:00","id":1202430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202324-sell-me-on-the-dragon-blooded?p=1202369#post1202369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah, it's not entire houses that are bad eggs.<br /> <br /> Like, the Ragara elders are up to some nasty shit. The younger members, who you'll end up playing, have no idea.<br /> <br /> So you can play a heroic Ragara scion who ends up being all &quot;omg grandpa wtf are you doing?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, there's a Marvel comic series called Runaways which I just started reading recently. The main premise is &quot;What if you and your friends found out that your parents were supervillains?&quot;<br /> <br /> After reading the Ragara entry, I could see that being a great premise for a DB game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T23:39:02-07:00","id":1202465,"title":"","content":"What this book seems to do well is focus a lot on the struggles of the dynasts, and the evils of a system rather than evils of the individual. Like for instance maybe you're really worried that a house Sesus legion is going to come storming into your home city and kill your whole family, if they can't be reasoned with and the civil war sparks hot. The thing is, you could really bolster your forces there with that big shipment of fire dust that your family managed to procure from a southern dust baron. It's your job to heroically go over there, see that the dust is loaded safely, battle off pirates who are debatably being paid off by house Sesus, and secure your family.<br /> <br /> The thing is, when you get there, the shipment is short. Some horrible monstrosity from the Wyld physically grabbed the whole last caravan wagon and made off with it. Images flash through your head of your family being put to the sword by those thugs, if diplomacy fails, so you need to get that back. While you're in the satrapy though, you might notice the dust baron is seriously treating his people badly. I mean your family is paying out the nose and he's milking it for all it's worth, he's a dick but you get why. However nothing is stopping you from being the best guy ever and getting that firedust back, rooting out some of the corruption in the dust baron's organization to help take a little pressure off the little guy, and then making it back in time to throw some weight behind your threats that if Sesus sends a legion to your home, they're losing that legion.<br /> <br /> The text kind of subtly implies that's most dynasts would just go there and make sure that's their family had absolutely everything it needed in the upcoming war, and that some might be bastards and drive the dust baron even harder to curry favour with their elders, others might be real true heroes, while others still might treat the whole thing as a vacation. Mostly some combination of all of those things and more will be true. You might even ask yourself if you could liberate the people from under the thumb of the dust baron, but that's damn hard, and if you don't get that dust somehow your family might pay with their lives. Or flip it, maybe you play the circle of DBs back on the isle carefully navigating the politics, trying desperately to hold off the war and clinging to a tiny sliver of hope that maybe there doesn't need to be one at all. <br /> <br /> If it just showed you the realm's oppression it'd be a charicature of an empire who's only purpose in play is to tear it down and build a something better. It does a great job of bringing things down to a close, human level, where even if you can see the whole system and the problems with it, the things and ideals that matter to you are all in danger, and you're probably not going to be a pure perfect hero all the time but navigating that is half the fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As to DBs playing second banana to other exalts it's basically not there at all. Anathema are scary, but they are as much obstacles to be overcome as predators that stalk you in the night. This book actually makes me want to play a Solar again because it actually feels like the Scarlet Dynasty has this huge weight, vastness, power to it, whereas the lone anathema out there really have nothing. House Mnemon doesn't deal with a random Solar, this small section of a portion of an army does that. It makes those few Solars who survive and thrive feel more special and accomplished. Surviving the Realm is a feat man, and ever present is the knowledge that probably the only reason you did survive is because the entire Realm wasn't after you.<br /> <br /> It also helps that that's basically the only time you're playing second banana. Other than your respected elders and fierce rivals the world is yours. You are utterly a class above. Where other women dream of seeing the ocean, or traveling across a mountain, you almost casually launch an expedition to the far reaches of the frontier to plumb ancient tombs and forgotten civilizations. Your concerns for food are how to feed your army, your concerns for dominance involve how far up the dynasty you can climb. You are at once incredibly individually powerful, and yet connected so deeply to something so much greater than yourself, struggling against others within it, as well as being bound by duty and the deepest kinship that any exalted experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> TLDR;<br /> I'm sorry this went on so long but it really is fantastic, I'm quite impressed and very excited to see more. Bringning the focus in tighter and making things more distinct really makes it feel more human and understandable. There's bad people, good people, most are a little of both, they're all in a shitty situation, and just maybe you and your friends have the power and wit to go out there and do something about it. Now go be a hero, whatever that means to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T12:50:52-07:00","id":1202689,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your responses; they've been helpful, and I very much appreciate them!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202324-sell-me-on-the-dragon-blooded?p=1202327#post1202327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Additionally, if you back it for $5, you'll be able to download the manuscript (that is, the full text, released in batches over the course of the KS) that's yours to keep, even if you dislike what you read and withdraw your pledge at the end. So there's nothing stopping you from just reading the book now and determining if you want to back it. Rich and team encourage this behavior. They want to earn your pledge, not make you assume it from others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your point is well-taken, and I think that I will do exactly that. Once I have a better sense of what's in the book and where Exalted generally and the Dragon-Blooded in particular are going; I will make a final call on backing the kickstarter.<br /> <br /> I will plan to post an update with my reasoning once I mage a final decision... for closure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}